From 76ac1749a22814cb38017d3b2c8f0256c4777109 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:15:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] Check far-word boundaries, operands, and loop-proof
 limits

Add direct 254/255 word endpoint controls, preserved base/index/MMO
checks, atomic/escape/call rejection, and a compact live-consumer IR case
whose known-bits bound does not depend on the loop matcher. Check the
feature-disabled byte lowering on that supported bounded input.

Cover reversed PHI operands, multiple external predecessors, a valid
narrow shift and the expression-recursion boundary. Terminate every
positive word-policy opcode explicitly, following the same contract as
the existing byte-range checks.

The broader no-A16 fallback probe reaches the already documented missing
s32/byte far-pointer bridge. Its diagnostic is retained as a prerequisite
scope limit; this test does not claim general A8 far-pointer support.

Review N8 additions: far-word-index-boundaries.mir checks that a word
store sharing the address rejects the whole group while a byte store folds
with the word load, and far-word-rep-sep.mir checks that REP/SEP insertion
sets X=1 before the folded word load after a 16-bit index instruction under
+mos-xy16. The mixed-order functions of far-word-policy.mir now pin the byte
sibling's opcode too, which the extended sensitivity runner found unchecked.
The boundary tests' OFF runs are gone with -mos-far-loop-range (review N5).

Validation: assertions-enabled exact-upstream extraction, 160 MOS
CodeGen/MC files pass and one pre-existing unconditional unsupported test.
Preparation and validation: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (session source
vscode), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session
01a0e67f-298f-7a21-80af-06f867085f84.

Review N5 and N8 test changes: Claude Code 2.1.285 (t4-opus-high agent), model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Skyq488smgqkyyzHrcCX7F
